================================================================================
SECTION 5 — SUPABASE BACKEND
================================================================================

TABLES (complete schema)

profiles
  id              uuid PK FK → auth.users.id
  role            text  CHECK IN ('patient','hospital_admin','concierge','admin')
  full_name       text
  email           text
  country         text
  phone           text
  language_pref   text  DEFAULT 'en'
  dob             date
  gender          text
  nationality     text
  passport_no     text
  passport_expiry date
  emergency_name  text
  emergency_phone text
  avatar_url      text
  status          text  DEFAULT 'active' CHECK IN ('active','suspended','deleted')
  created_at      timestamptz DEFAULT now()

hospitals
  id              uuid PK
  name            text NOT NULL
  city            text
  state           text
  address         text
  description     text
  accreditations  text[]
  specialties     text[]
  rating          numeric DEFAULT 0
  review_count    int DEFAULT 0
  images          text[]
  partner_status  text DEFAULT 'pending' CHECK IN ('pending','approved','suspended','rejected')
  admin_id        uuid FK → profiles.id
  created_at      timestamptz

doctors
  id              uuid PK
  hospital_id     uuid FK → hospitals.id
  name            text
  specialty       text
  degree          text
  bio             text
  photo_url       text
  languages       text[]
  experience_yrs  int
  success_rate    numeric
  is_verified     bool DEFAULT false
  created_at      timestamptz

treatments
  id              uuid PK
  name            text
  slug            text UNIQUE
  description     text
  category        text
  avg_cost_min    numeric
  avg_cost_max    numeric
  recovery_days   int
  success_rate    numeric
  created_at      timestamptz

packages
  id              uuid PK
  hospital_id     uuid FK → hospitals.id
  treatment_id    uuid FK → treatments.id
  title           text
  hotel_included  bool DEFAULT false
  hotel_tier      int
  transfer        bool DEFAULT false
  translator      bool DEFAULT false
  visa_assistance bool DEFAULT false
  price_inr       numeric
  duration_days   int
  is_available    bool DEFAULT true
  created_at      timestamptz

bookings
  id              uuid PK
  patient_id      uuid FK → profiles.id
  package_id      uuid FK → packages.id
  hospital_id     uuid FK → hospitals.id
  doctor_id       uuid FK → doctors.id
  treatment_id    uuid FK → treatments.id
  concierge_id    uuid FK → profiles.id
  status          text DEFAULT 'pending'
                  CHECK IN ('draft','pending','confirmed',
                  'in_progress','completed','cancelled')
  travel_month    text
  travel_flexible bool
  companions      int DEFAULT 0
  medical_summary text
  admin_notes     text
  total_amount    numeric
  created_at      timestamptz

payments
  id              uuid PK
  booking_id      uuid FK → bookings.id
  amount_inr      numeric
  amount_usd      numeric
  status          text CHECK IN ('success','failed','pending')
  demo_last4      text
  created_at      timestamptz
  NOTE: No real card data. Demo only.

messages
  id              uuid PK
  booking_id      uuid FK → bookings.id
  sender_id       uuid FK → profiles.id
  content         text
  is_urgent       bool DEFAULT false
  attachment_url  text
  created_at      timestamptz DEFAULT now()

documents
  id              uuid PK
  patient_id      uuid FK → profiles.id
  booking_id      uuid FK → bookings.id
  file_path       text
  file_name       text
  file_type       text
  file_size_kb    int
  uploaded_at     timestamptz DEFAULT now()

reviews
  id              uuid PK
  patient_id      uuid FK → profiles.id
  hospital_id     uuid FK → hospitals.id
  doctor_id       uuid FK → doctors.id
  booking_id      uuid FK → bookings.id
  rating          int CHECK (rating BETWEEN 1 AND 5)
  comment         text
  is_published    bool DEFAULT false
  created_at      timestamptz

blog_posts
  id              uuid PK
  title           text
  slug            text UNIQUE
  body            text
  featured_image  text
  tags            text[]
  status          text CHECK IN ('draft','published')
  author_id       uuid FK → profiles.id
  published_at    timestamptz
  created_at      timestamptz

support_tickets
  id              uuid PK
  patient_id      uuid FK → profiles.id
  booking_id      uuid FK → bookings.id
  issue           text
  status          text DEFAULT 'open' CHECK IN ('open','in_progress','resolved')
  admin_reply     text
  created_at      timestamptz

ROW-LEVEL SECURITY POLICIES

profiles       : SELECT/UPDATE own row; admin SELECT all
hospitals      : SELECT approved (public); hospital_admin UPDATE own; admin ALL
doctors        : SELECT all (public); hospital_admin INSERT/UPDATE for own hospital
treatments     : SELECT all (public); admin INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE
packages       : SELECT available (public); hospital_admin manage own; admin ALL
bookings       : patient SELECT own; hospital_admin SELECT linked; admin ALL
payments       : patient SELECT own; admin SELECT all
messages       : participants of booking only (patient + concierge + hospital_admin)
documents      : patient SELECT own; concierge SELECT if booking assigned; admin ALL
reviews        : SELECT published (public); INSERT by patient with completed booking
blog_posts     : SELECT published (public); admin ALL
support_tickets: patient SELECT own; admin ALL

SUPABASE STORAGE BUCKETS
  patient-documents  : private, RLS — patient + assigned concierge only
  hospital-images    : public read, hospital_admin write own
  doctor-photos      : public read, hospital_admin write
  blog-images        : public read, admin write
  avatars            : public read, user write own


================================================================================
SECTION 6 — AUTH & ROLES
================================================================================

ROLES
  patient         Default on signup
  hospital_admin  Assigned by admin after hospital approval
  concierge       Assigned by admin (internal MediTrip staff)
  admin           Created once at /1234/admin/setup

ROUTE PROTECTION RULES
  /book/*              → patient only → else /login?returnTo=...
  /dashboard/*         → patient only → else /login?returnTo=...
  /partner/*           → hospital_admin only → else /unauthorized
  /1234/admin/*        → admin only → else /1234/admin/login

SUPABASE AUTH SETUP
  Email/password: enabled
  Google OAuth: enabled (optional for patients)
  Email confirmation: enabled (OTP)
  Session: JWT, 7-day expiry, auto-refresh
  Admin password reset: manual (update via Supabase dashboard — not self-service)


================================================================================
SECTION 7 — CAPACITOR (ANDROID)
================================================================================

HOW IT WORKS
  Same Vite + React codebase
  Capacitor wraps the built web app into a WebView Android app
  No separate mobile codebase needed

SETUP STEPS (for developer)
  1. npm install @capacitor/core @capacitor/cli @capacitor/android
  2. npx cap init MediTrip com.meditrip.app
  3. vite build (builds /dist)
  4. npx cap add android
  5. npx cap copy android
  6. npx cap open android (opens Android Studio)
  7. Build APK from Android Studio (Generate Signed APK)

capacitor.config.ts
  appId     : com.meditrip.app
  appName   : MediTrip
  webDir    : dist
  server.androidScheme: https

CAPACITOR PLUGINS TO INSTALL
  @capacitor/camera         (patient profile photo upload)
  @capacitor/filesystem     (local file access on Android)
  @capacitor/push-notifications (Phase 2 — booking alerts)
  @capacitor/share          (share hospital/package links)
  @capacitor/haptics        (button tap feedback)
  @capacitor/status-bar     (set status bar sky blue)

MOBILE-SPECIFIC BEHAVIOR
  Bottom tab navigation (not sidebar) on screens < 768px
  Swipe gestures on galleries and carousels
  File upload uses device camera or gallery picker
  WhatsApp links open native app
  All links to external pages open in in-app browser


================================================================================
SECTION 8 — VERCEL DEPLOYMENT
================================================================================

SETUP
  Connect GitHub repo to Vercel
  Framework preset: Vite
  Build command: npm run build
  Output directory: dist
  Install command: npm install

vercel.json
  {
    "rewrites": [{ "source": "/(.*)", "destination": "/index.html" }]
  }
  (Required for React Router — all routes return index.html)

ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES (set in Vercel dashboard)
  VITE_SUPABASE_URL           your Supabase project URL
  VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY      your Supabase anon key
  VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY    Google Maps Embed API key
  VITE_APP_NAME               MediTrip
  VITE_WHATSAPP_NUMBER        +91XXXXXXXXXX
  VITE_CONTACT_EMAIL          support@meditrip.in

DEPLOYMENT FLOW
  Push to main branch → Vercel auto-deploys in ~60 seconds
  Pull requests → Vercel creates preview URL automatically
  Custom domain: add in Vercel project settings


================================================================================
SECTION 9 — KEY TECHNICAL DECISIONS
================================================================================

DECISION                   CHOICE                    REASON
State management           Zustand                   Simple, no boilerplate,
                                                     works well with Vite
Form management            React Hook Form + Zod     Type-safe validation,
                                                     minimal re-renders
UI components              shadcn/ui + Tailwind CSS  Accessible, customizable,
                                                     no style conflicts
Charts (admin)             Recharts                  Lightweight, React-native,
                                                     no jQuery dependency
Rich text (blog)           React-Quill               Simple, no server needed
Maps                       Google Maps Embed API     No SDK needed, just iframe,
                                                     no billing complexity
i18n                       i18next                   Industry standard,
                                                     Vite plugin available
Date handling              date-fns                  Lightweight, tree-shakeable
HTTP client                Supabase JS SDK only      No Axios needed —
                                                     Supabase handles all calls
PDF generation             @react-pdf/renderer       Client-side receipts,
                                                     no server needed
Icons                      Lucide React              Consistent, tree-shakeable,
                                                     used by shadcn/ui


================================================================================
SECTION 10 — NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
================================================================================

PERFORMANCE
  LCP < 2.5 seconds on 4G mobile
  Route-based code splitting (Vite lazy imports)
  Images: WebP format, lazy loading
  Fonts: preloaded, subset only Latin + Devanagari + Bengali

SECURITY
  Supabase RLS on every single table — no exceptions
  No secrets in frontend code (all via VITE_ env vars which are public,
  but anon key is safe with RLS enforced)
  File access via Supabase signed URLs (1-hour expiry)
  Admin route at /1234/admin — obscure URL as first layer of protection
  HTTPS enforced (Vercel default)

ACCESSIBILITY
  WCAG 2.1 AA minimum
  All interactive elements keyboard-navigable
  ARIA labels on icons and image-only buttons
  Minimum 4.5:1 contrast ratio (sky blue on white passes)

GDPR
  Cookie consent banner on first visit
  "Delete My Account" in patient profile (soft delete + data anonymization)
  Privacy Policy and Terms pages linked in footer
  No third-party analytics in Phase 1 (only Vercel Analytics, privacy-safe)

SUPPORTED BROWSERS / OS
  Web: Chrome 90+, Safari 14+, Firefox 88+, Edge 90+
  Android: API 24+ (Android 7.0 Nougat and above) via Capacitor


================================================================================
SECTION 11 — ADMIN SETUP GUIDE
================================================================================

FIRST-TIME ADMIN CREATION
  1. Deploy the application to Vercel
  2. Visit: yourdomain.com/1234/admin/setup
  3. Enter: Admin Email + Password (choose strong password)
  4. Click "Create Admin Account"
  5. Supabase creates user with role = admin
  6. /1234/admin/setup becomes inaccessible (redirects to /1234/admin/login)
  7. Login at: yourdomain.com/1234/admin/login

ADMIN PASSWORD CHANGE
  Not available in the app (by design — admin is fixed)
  To change password: go to Supabase Dashboard → Authentication → Users
  Find admin email → "Send Password Reset" or update directly in SQL editor

ADDING CONCIERGE USERS
  Admin creates account manually in Supabase Auth with role = concierge
  Or: add a "Create Concierge" form in /1234/admin/settings (optional)


